WEBVTT

1
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:19,888
(man grunting,
punching bag chains rattling)

2
00:00:19,954 --> 00:00:23,725
(dark, tense music)

3
00:00:26,928 --> 00:00:28,563
(loud grunt)

4
00:00:36,771 --> 00:00:38,006
(loud grunt)

5
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:39,741
(machine guns firing)
- Don't move!

6
00:00:43,811 --> 00:00:45,445
(distant muffled shouting)

7
00:00:49,984 --> 00:00:54,288
(sinister music peaks
then fades)

8
00:01:04,264 --> 00:01:06,768
(shrill sinister music builds)

9
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:10,638
(music fades)

10
00:01:13,908 --> 00:01:15,309
(lighter clicks)

11
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:36,531
- Not gonna ask how I found ya?

12
00:01:36,598 --> 00:01:39,834
- You can find anyone nowadays.
It's not that impressive.

13
00:01:42,670 --> 00:01:46,473
- Yeah. S'pose that is
fair enough, isn't it?

14
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:52,312
Look, Knox is alive.
And we found him.

15
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:57,652
So, we're putting together
a team to go save his ass.

16
00:01:57,719 --> 00:01:59,319
We need a fourth.

17
00:01:59,386 --> 00:02:01,990
More importantly,
I need a point man.

18
00:02:02,056 --> 00:02:03,591
You're the only one I trust.

19
00:02:03,658 --> 00:02:06,259
And you're the only one
that's worked in the unit,

20
00:02:06,326 --> 00:02:08,730
back when Knox was still around.

21
00:02:08,796 --> 00:02:09,797
- Yeah, I remember.

22
00:02:09,864 --> 00:02:12,499
Rest of them are fucking dead
because of you.

23
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:17,705
- We need
to bring him home, mate.

24
00:02:19,574 --> 00:02:22,710
- Wade and Jace agree to this?
- Of course they do.

25
00:02:24,411 --> 00:02:25,647
We're not gonna
leave a man behind.

26
00:02:25,713 --> 00:02:28,082
- Let me make something
clear to you.

27
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:30,785
My conscience is clean.

28
00:02:30,852 --> 00:02:33,021
Afghanistan...

29
00:02:33,087 --> 00:02:34,989
that shit was on you
and Anderson,

30
00:02:35,056 --> 00:02:36,958
and no one else.

31
00:02:37,025 --> 00:02:39,493
Knox would agree with me.

32
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:43,497
He was a good man.
- He is a good man.

33
00:02:43,564 --> 00:02:46,634
That's why we need
to bring him home.

34
00:02:48,069 --> 00:02:49,804
Look, here's an address.

35
00:02:53,608 --> 00:02:57,177
If you decide to join us,
and I hope you do,

36
00:02:57,244 --> 00:02:59,446
meet me there tomorrow morning.

37
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,583
It was good seeing
you again, Marcus.

38
00:03:17,065 --> 00:03:18,700
(tense music)

39
00:03:29,276 --> 00:03:31,779
(siren chirps briefly)

40
00:04:00,273 --> 00:04:02,176
(somber music)

41
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:05,613
(distant sirens wailing)

42
00:04:16,124 --> 00:04:17,825
(shouting)

43
00:04:20,561 --> 00:04:22,496
(shouting, machine gun firing)

44
00:04:28,236 --> 00:04:30,805
(waves rushing)

45
00:04:35,143 --> 00:04:37,612
(soft tense music)

46
00:04:44,185 --> 00:04:45,953
- So, what now, Briggs?

47
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,489
- We're going to Mexico.

48
00:04:49,557 --> 00:04:51,324
We're going to a town
called Durango.

49
00:04:51,391 --> 00:04:54,162
From there, half a day's walk.

50
00:04:54,228 --> 00:04:55,563
- How we going in?

51
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:59,600
- It's a covert operation,
snatch and grab.

52
00:04:59,667 --> 00:05:02,503
- Is Anderson in on this?
- She is.

53
00:05:05,573 --> 00:05:08,509
- When do we leave?
- Right now.

54
00:05:12,246 --> 00:05:14,582
(plane roars overhead)

55
00:05:21,589 --> 00:05:23,724
- And I think this is it,
Captain.

56
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:33,901
- Yeah, this is it.

57
00:05:34,836 --> 00:05:38,573
Anderson, we have confirmation
on the facility. Over.

58
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:42,009
- Roger that.
Proceed to the facility.

59
00:05:42,076 --> 00:05:43,845
- Wade, Jace,

60
00:05:43,911 --> 00:05:46,180
come forward to this position
and overwatch.

61
00:05:46,247 --> 00:05:50,017
Marcus and I'll move forward
into the facility. Roger that?

62
00:05:50,084 --> 00:05:53,521
<i>(Wade, over radio): Roger that.</i>
<i>We're on the way.</i>

63
00:05:53,588 --> 00:05:56,057
- Roger that. Moving now out.

64
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,806
(soft tense music continues)

65
00:06:18,579 --> 00:06:21,349
(Anderson): Two Tangos
are approaching.

66
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:22,950
Use your discretion.

67
00:06:26,153 --> 00:06:27,788
(in Spanish)

68
00:06:48,609 --> 00:06:50,011
- I'll take
the one on the right.

69
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:53,648
You take the one on the left.
- Roger that.

70
00:07:00,154 --> 00:07:01,756
(music builds)

71
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:03,824
(bullets whiz)

72
00:07:07,328 --> 00:07:08,829
- Clear.

73
00:07:20,541 --> 00:07:22,475
<i>(Briggs): Both targets</i>
<i>neutralized.</i>

74
00:07:22,543 --> 00:07:23,811
<i>(Anderson): Are they cartel?</i>

75
00:07:23,878 --> 00:07:26,647
<i>(Briggs): Affirmative.</i>
<i>(Anderson): Roger that, Captain.</i>

76
00:07:30,918 --> 00:07:32,687
No sign of life
on the outside, Captain.

77
00:07:32,753 --> 00:07:34,555
<i>(Briggs): Roger that, Anderson.</i>

78
00:07:34,622 --> 00:07:35,957
(Anderson): Proceed
with caution.

79
00:07:36,023 --> 00:07:38,125
<i>(Briggs): Wade, move forward</i>
<i>into the facility.</i>

80
00:07:38,192 --> 00:07:40,962
<i>(Wade): Roger that.</i>
<i>Proceeding to the facility.</i>

81
00:07:47,234 --> 00:07:49,170
<i>(Anderson): You've entered</i>
<i>the main level of the facility.</i>

82
00:07:49,236 --> 00:07:51,672
<i>You should have entry points</i>
<i>to the upper and lower floors</i>

83
00:07:51,739 --> 00:07:54,008
<i>from there.</i>
(Briggs): Roger that, Anderson.

84
00:07:56,544 --> 00:07:58,746
Hold left, push right.

85
00:08:02,216 --> 00:08:03,751
Move.

86
00:08:08,189 --> 00:08:09,724
Clear.

87
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,894
Go.

88
00:08:18,733 --> 00:08:20,067
<i>(Anderson): Captain,</i>
<i>do whatever you can</i>

89
00:08:20,134 --> 00:08:22,570
<i>to find his whereabouts.</i>
<i>Gather any information you can.</i>

90
00:08:22,636 --> 00:08:24,138
<i>(Briggs): Affirmative.</i>

91
00:08:45,326 --> 00:08:47,495
(radar beeping)

92
00:08:47,561 --> 00:08:49,263
<i>(Briggs): Room right.</i>

93
00:08:51,232 --> 00:08:53,934
(tense music)

94
00:09:08,449 --> 00:09:10,818
Clear. Moving upstairs.

95
00:09:32,907 --> 00:09:34,442
Clear.
<i>(Anderson): Have you reached</i>

96
00:09:34,509 --> 00:09:35,743
<i>the second story yet,</i>
<i>Captain?</i>

97
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,878
(Briggs): Roger.
Second floor is clear.

98
00:09:37,945 --> 00:09:40,281
- Any sign of Tango 6?
<i>(Briggs): No sign of Tango 6.</i>

99
00:09:40,948 --> 00:09:42,850
<i>Continuing on.</i>

100
00:09:51,759 --> 00:09:53,861
Keep it tight, boys.

101
00:09:59,667 --> 00:10:01,936
Can you smell that?

102
00:10:30,599 --> 00:10:34,034
- Fuck. You seeing this?

103
00:10:35,537 --> 00:10:38,739
- Go or die. It's a warning.

104
00:10:38,806 --> 00:10:41,108
- Is that Knox, Captain?

105
00:10:43,377 --> 00:10:45,045
- No, it isn't.

106
00:10:45,112 --> 00:10:47,348
Knox wouldn't have
gone out like that.

107
00:10:50,651 --> 00:10:52,119
We're gonna find him.

108
00:10:54,822 --> 00:10:57,158
All right. On me, boys.

109
00:11:01,695 --> 00:11:04,165
(low ominous music)

110
00:11:10,905 --> 00:11:13,040
(sharp inhale and exhale)

111
00:11:17,612 --> 00:11:19,380
(ominous music building)

112
00:11:24,653 --> 00:11:27,121
(flesh squelches)

113
00:11:38,098 --> 00:11:38,933
<i>(Anderson): We're reading that</i>
<i>there are multiple</i>

114
00:11:38,999 --> 00:11:40,868
<i>tangos ahead. You're closing in.</i>

115
00:11:42,637 --> 00:11:47,141
(men laughing,
speaking Spanish)

116
00:11:51,745 --> 00:11:54,281
(indistinct chatter continues)

117
00:11:58,285 --> 00:11:59,386
(whistle)

118
00:12:01,322 --> 00:12:02,389
(whistle)

119
00:12:14,669 --> 00:12:16,270
(tense music)

120
00:12:17,738 --> 00:12:20,307
(muffled gag)

121
00:12:40,961 --> 00:12:43,364
- Don't even think about it.

122
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,299
(in Spanish)

123
00:12:56,343 --> 00:12:57,512
(coughs)

124
00:12:58,546 --> 00:13:00,281
- Last chance, compadres.

125
00:13:11,191 --> 00:13:13,294
(Briggs): Marcus,
shut them the fuck up.

126
00:13:18,932 --> 00:13:21,035
- All right, get 'em up.

127
00:13:22,504 --> 00:13:24,038
(gasps)

128
00:13:24,673 --> 00:13:26,307
(bullet whizzes)

129
00:13:27,542 --> 00:13:29,276
(gurgling)

130
00:13:31,378 --> 00:13:35,249
(Briggs): He's bleeding out way
too fucking much. Goddamnit!

131
00:13:48,763 --> 00:13:50,998
Except for these, he's clean.

132
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,402
- Don't wanna waste 'em, right?

133
00:14:00,874 --> 00:14:03,277
- He's got nothing, Briggs.

134
00:14:05,946 --> 00:14:08,182
This doesn't feel right.
Something's off.

135
00:14:08,248 --> 00:14:10,851
- We've got two more levels
to clear

136
00:14:10,918 --> 00:14:13,220
and we need to keep moving.

137
00:14:14,723 --> 00:14:15,590
- Contact.

138
00:14:18,092 --> 00:14:20,994
(Briggs): Anderson,
contact. Over.

139
00:14:21,061 --> 00:14:23,464
- Roger that.
You're free to engage.

140
00:14:23,531 --> 00:14:26,568
(goggles whirring)
<i>- Roger that. Going dark.</i>

141
00:14:28,737 --> 00:14:31,038
(tense music)

142
00:14:37,846 --> 00:14:39,614
(beeping)

143
00:14:44,753 --> 00:14:46,453
- Hey!
(gunshot)

144
00:14:50,457 --> 00:14:51,425
(gunfire)

145
00:14:51,492 --> 00:14:52,292
(grunts)

146
00:14:57,464 --> 00:14:58,465
- Move.

147
00:15:19,453 --> 00:15:21,656
(Briggs): Shotgun. Take cover.
(shotgun blasts)

148
00:15:22,089 --> 00:15:23,558
(automatic gunfire)

149
00:15:25,727 --> 00:15:26,728
Clear.

150
00:15:26,795 --> 00:15:27,896
- Captain.

151
00:15:27,961 --> 00:15:29,229
<i>We spotted multiple tangos</i>

152
00:15:29,296 --> 00:15:31,098
heading into the facility
right now.

153
00:15:31,165 --> 00:15:32,600
You're running out of time.

154
00:15:32,667 --> 00:15:34,101
<i>(Briggs): Affirmative.</i>

155
00:15:44,144 --> 00:15:46,881
- What's the plan, Captain?

156
00:15:46,947 --> 00:15:48,949
This place gives me the creeps.

157
00:15:49,016 --> 00:15:51,485
- What in the hell
is this place?

158
00:15:54,188 --> 00:15:56,423
- Used to be a church.

159
00:15:57,659 --> 00:15:58,693
- Told you.

160
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,461
- Quiet.

161
00:16:13,808 --> 00:16:14,975
<i>(Anderson): Any sign of Tango 6?</i>

162
00:16:15,042 --> 00:16:17,277
- No, but we're not alone.

163
00:16:17,344 --> 00:16:19,112
Get the fuck on the ground!

164
00:16:19,179 --> 00:16:22,115
I will fucking shoot you!
Do you understand?!

165
00:16:22,182 --> 00:16:23,852
(hollow breathing)

166
00:16:23,918 --> 00:16:25,352
- Multiple tangos.
Should we engage?

167
00:16:25,419 --> 00:16:27,287
- Briggs, what is it?
What do you see?

168
00:16:27,354 --> 00:16:28,857
I got a guy
coming up the stairs.

169
00:16:28,923 --> 00:16:30,090
Identify yourself right now!

170
00:16:30,157 --> 00:16:33,260
Put that shit down!
Put that shit down!

171
00:16:33,928 --> 00:16:35,763
- Grenades, get down!
- Open fire!

172
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:37,431
(gunfire)

173
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,834
(loud blast)

174
00:16:39,901 --> 00:16:41,034
(high-pitched ringing)

175
00:16:41,101 --> 00:16:43,705
(muffled echoing shouting)

176
00:16:43,771 --> 00:16:46,440
(distorted music)

177
00:16:46,508 --> 00:16:47,742
- Briggs!

178
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,745
I need you to get your ass
on the fucking ground!

179
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:53,948
(gunshot)

180
00:16:54,014 --> 00:16:55,482
(choking)

181
00:16:55,550 --> 00:16:57,785
<i>(Anderson): Captain Briggs,</i>
<i>can you hear me?</i>

182
00:16:57,852 --> 00:17:00,722
(hollow inhale)

183
00:17:00,788 --> 00:17:02,022
I repeat, can you hear me?

184
00:17:02,089 --> 00:17:04,024
(Briggs): Die! Fucking die!

185
00:17:04,091 --> 00:17:06,260
- Wade? Marcus? Do you copy?

186
00:17:07,529 --> 00:17:08,530
(grunts)

187
00:17:09,229 --> 00:17:11,666
(distorted music continues)

188
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:14,602
(muffled choking)

189
00:17:18,573 --> 00:17:19,674
(coughing)

190
00:17:21,074 --> 00:17:22,877
(muffled breathing)

191
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:25,178
(gunshot)
- Anderson, do you copy?

192
00:17:25,245 --> 00:17:27,882
Anderson? Somebody?

193
00:17:27,949 --> 00:17:29,449
(grunts)

194
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:34,889
- Captain Briggs,
can you hear me?

195
00:17:34,956 --> 00:17:36,356
- They can't hear you.

196
00:17:36,423 --> 00:17:38,660
Our communication's
been cut off.

197
00:17:38,726 --> 00:17:40,227
- Marcus!

198
00:17:40,294 --> 00:17:41,896
- Well then do your job
and get them

199
00:17:41,963 --> 00:17:43,196
back online with me.

200
00:17:43,263 --> 00:17:44,999
We're all they have,
for Christ's sake.

201
00:17:45,065 --> 00:17:46,634
(high-pitched ringing)

202
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:49,871
(gun blasts)

203
00:17:49,938 --> 00:17:51,706
(coughing)

204
00:18:03,083 --> 00:18:04,251
(monitor beeping)

205
00:18:04,318 --> 00:18:08,523
(sighs)
Fuck this. God.

206
00:18:09,691 --> 00:18:12,694
General, sir, I need to speak
with you. It's urgent.

207
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:15,262
- Yeah, I'll be with you
in a moment, Agent Anderson.

208
00:18:15,329 --> 00:18:17,164
Isaac, can you pull
this up on radar?

209
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:19,801
- Yes, sir.
- We lost them.

210
00:18:19,867 --> 00:18:21,134
The whole team went dark.

211
00:18:21,201 --> 00:18:22,369
If I can get an evac team
right now,

212
00:18:22,436 --> 00:18:24,505
they might still have a chance.

213
00:18:27,207 --> 00:18:28,743
- What do you mean
the team went dark?

214
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:29,844
- Comms went dark.

215
00:18:32,412 --> 00:18:34,181
- Give the agent and I
a moment, would you?

216
00:18:34,247 --> 00:18:36,450
- Yes, sir.
- Walk with me.

217
00:18:36,517 --> 00:18:38,318
(Anderson): We spent months
tracking them down,

218
00:18:38,385 --> 00:18:40,320
scouting out the area,
tracking Knox down.

219
00:18:40,387 --> 00:18:41,689
(General): This isn't the first
time they've engaged

220
00:18:41,756 --> 00:18:43,625
with cartel forces.
- If I can just get

221
00:18:43,691 --> 00:18:46,326
one extraction team,
whichever one that you want.

222
00:18:46,393 --> 00:18:49,063
- Those SEALs were
your extraction team!

223
00:18:49,129 --> 00:18:50,565
They were sent in to get Knox.

224
00:18:50,632 --> 00:18:52,800
How can I justify sending
any more men

225
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:56,704
over this wild goose chase?
- You know damn well why.

226
00:18:58,338 --> 00:19:00,742
- It's been three years.

227
00:19:01,643 --> 00:19:04,646
Lieutenant Knox has become
nothing more than a Bigfoot.

228
00:19:05,847 --> 00:19:07,280
If that SEAL team is KIA

229
00:19:07,347 --> 00:19:09,449
because of your negligence,

230
00:19:09,517 --> 00:19:12,553
I promise, this ghost hunt
will end now.

231
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:16,390
I won't authorize any more men
dying over this.

232
00:19:23,196 --> 00:19:25,033
(intense music resonating)

233
00:19:25,099 --> 00:19:27,602
(distorted shouting)

234
00:19:28,368 --> 00:19:29,904
<i>(man): We never stop fighting.</i>

235
00:19:31,139 --> 00:19:32,540
<i>Marcus.</i>

236
00:19:32,607 --> 00:19:34,742
(gasping)

237
00:19:36,044 --> 00:19:37,545
<i>Marcus.</i>

238
00:19:37,612 --> 00:19:38,746
(gasping)

239
00:19:41,381 --> 00:19:44,384
<i>These dogs chasing cars.</i>

240
00:19:45,053 --> 00:19:45,953
(calm music plays briefly)

241
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,454
(birds chirping)

242
00:19:48,122 --> 00:19:52,325
<i>(man): Marcus, you are a wolf.</i>
<i>You're a wolf.</i>

243
00:19:52,392 --> 00:19:55,462
(breathing heavily)

244
00:19:58,231 --> 00:20:00,101
- Is he wounded?

245
00:20:00,168 --> 00:20:03,571
- No. One was wounded.

246
00:20:03,638 --> 00:20:04,471
- No.

247
00:20:04,539 --> 00:20:06,206
- They went out
without a fight,

248
00:20:06,273 --> 00:20:08,643
but we did what we had to do.

249
00:20:10,511 --> 00:20:13,548
- And what will come
of this thing?

250
00:20:13,614 --> 00:20:15,315
- I'm sorry, sir.
I didn't think we...

251
00:20:15,382 --> 00:20:17,719
(muffled gagging)

252
00:20:23,524 --> 00:20:25,860
<i>(man): We never stop fighting.</i>

253
00:20:33,167 --> 00:20:34,802
- Feed him to the dogs.

254
00:20:36,003 --> 00:20:38,606
Put him with the others.

255
00:20:38,673 --> 00:20:41,743
Commodus would like to see
how he does in the arena.

256
00:20:45,412 --> 00:20:48,649
(sinister music peaks
then fades)

257
00:20:59,026 --> 00:21:00,494
