01:14:57,898 --> 01:15:00,500
He showed me the path
to greatness

1045
01:15:00,568 --> 01:15:02,636
by unlocking my true potential

1046
01:15:02,703 --> 01:15:04,572
in a fight
of uncanny proportions.

1047
01:15:04,638 --> 01:15:07,008
(music swells)

1048
01:15:09,710 --> 01:15:11,712
It was in this very arena

1049
01:15:11,779 --> 01:15:15,383
that I battled
my closest friend,

1050
01:15:15,449 --> 01:15:16,784
my brother...

1051
01:15:20,054 --> 01:15:20,988
(exhales)

1052
01:15:23,090 --> 01:15:24,191
...to his death.

1053
01:15:30,331 --> 01:15:31,799
- No.

1054
01:15:34,435 --> 01:15:37,506
- Let the fight begin!

1055
01:15:37,571 --> 01:15:39,974
(uproarious cheering)

1056
01:15:41,609 --> 01:15:44,011
(overlapping shouting)

1057
01:15:54,055 --> 01:15:56,123
(grunting)

1058
01:16:08,402 --> 01:16:09,236
(grunts)

1059
01:16:09,303 --> 01:16:11,338
(shouting continues)

1060
01:16:11,405 --> 01:16:13,841
(lands punches, grunting)

1061
01:16:21,282 --> 01:16:24,952
- You gotta stop, Briggs.
- You don't get it, do you?

1062
01:16:25,853 --> 01:16:30,091
If both of us live,
both of us die.

1063
01:16:32,326 --> 01:16:34,161
(grunting)

1064
01:16:41,202 --> 01:16:42,903
(loud scream)

1065
01:16:43,471 --> 01:16:46,273
(onlookers shouting)

1066
01:16:52,713 --> 01:16:55,316
(Briggs): You have to do it,
Marcus.

1067
01:16:56,350 --> 01:16:58,319
(heart beating)

1068
01:16:58,385 --> 01:16:59,086
<i>- Marcus...</i>

1069
01:17:00,287 --> 01:17:01,355
- Die!

1070
01:17:02,389 --> 01:17:03,791
- ... you are a wolf.

1071
01:17:04,391 --> 01:17:06,360
(blood spurts, groans)

1072
01:17:08,563 --> 01:17:11,265
(onlookers shouting)

1073
01:17:11,332 --> 01:17:12,900
(gurgling)

1074
01:17:24,645 --> 01:17:26,280
- What say you, Commodus?

1075
01:17:27,047 --> 01:17:29,817
- I say, what's a trophy
without a head?

1076
01:17:29,884 --> 01:17:33,053
(onlookers exclaiming)

1077
01:17:34,788 --> 01:17:37,825
(all shouting)

1078
01:17:41,729 --> 01:17:44,899
- Ah. Finish him.

1079
01:17:46,700 --> 01:17:48,836
(onlookers shouting)

1080
01:17:50,704 --> 01:17:53,073
- Are you ready, my son?

1081
01:17:54,408 --> 01:17:55,943
- Yes.

1082
01:17:58,379 --> 01:17:59,313
(thuds)

1083
01:18:07,522 --> 01:18:09,223
(rally cry)

1084
01:18:11,392 --> 01:18:13,027
(machine guns firing)

1085
01:18:15,530 --> 01:18:18,132
(sinister music)

1086
01:18:19,300 --> 01:18:21,068
(shouting)

1087
01:18:29,544 --> 01:18:30,911
(Marcus grunts)

1088
01:18:31,613 --> 01:18:34,381
(gunshots crack)

1089
01:18:35,749 --> 01:18:37,117
(machine gunfire)

1090
01:18:40,287 --> 01:18:42,389
(gunshots crack)

1091
01:18:46,628 --> 01:18:48,462
(tense music)

1092
01:18:59,306 --> 01:19:01,175
(gunshots crack)

1093
01:19:01,875 --> 01:19:04,979
(machine gun fires rapidly)

1094
01:19:06,747 --> 01:19:09,450
(sweeping ominous music)

1095
01:19:09,517 --> 01:19:11,318
(gunshots crack)

1096
01:19:11,785 --> 01:19:13,387
(gun clicking)

1097
01:19:14,689 --> 01:19:17,124
(grunting, punching)

1098
01:19:19,426 --> 01:19:21,295
(breathing heavily)

1099
01:19:22,796 --> 01:19:24,331
(grunting)

1100
01:19:27,901 --> 01:19:30,104
(machine gun fires rapidly)

1101
01:19:33,307 --> 01:19:36,777
(Butcher): Your fate,
dear Brutus,

1102
01:19:36,844 --> 01:19:39,446
lies not in the stars...

1103
01:19:39,514 --> 01:19:40,948
(groaning)

1104
01:19:41,015 --> 01:19:44,418
..but within ourselves.

1105
01:19:44,485 --> 01:19:45,486
(knife swishes)

1106
01:19:47,388 --> 01:19:48,556
(groans)

1107
01:19:48,623 --> 01:19:51,058
(blood spurting, gasping)

1108
01:19:57,464 --> 01:19:59,233
(breathing heavily)

1109
01:20:04,471 --> 01:20:06,006
(spits)

1110
01:20:07,408 --> 01:20:09,476
(tense music)

1111
01:20:19,320 --> 01:20:21,589
(Wade): Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!
(men shouting)

1112
01:20:21,656 --> 01:20:23,223
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

1113
01:20:23,290 --> 01:20:25,426
What the hell
are you doing here?

1114
01:20:25,492 --> 01:20:27,061
- Where's Knox?

1115
01:20:27,127 --> 01:20:29,096
- Are you the extraction team?
Where's the rest of 'em?

1116
01:20:29,163 --> 01:20:31,666
- We're all that's left.
- Shit.

1117
01:20:31,733 --> 01:20:33,635
- Where's Knox, Wade?

1118
01:20:33,702 --> 01:20:35,603
- Marcus went after him.

1119
01:20:35,670 --> 01:20:38,072
And Knox, he's gone mad.

1120
01:20:39,774 --> 01:20:41,141
- What about Briggs?

1121
01:20:41,208 --> 01:20:43,177
- Jace and Briggs,
they didn't make it.

1122
01:20:43,243 --> 01:20:46,113
- I'm sorry it had
to go this way, Wade.

1123
01:20:46,614 --> 01:20:48,516
(gunshots firing)

1124
01:20:53,987 --> 01:20:55,389
(Wade): Anderson...

1125
01:20:55,456 --> 01:20:56,558
(gunshot cracks)

1126
01:21:03,130 --> 01:21:05,199
- We need to find
Marcus and Knox.

1127
01:21:07,234 --> 01:21:09,370
(Knox): We aren't good men,
Marcus.

1128
01:21:09,436 --> 01:21:10,772
None of us.

1129
01:21:10,839 --> 01:21:12,507
This is where we belong.

1130
01:21:12,574 --> 01:21:13,941
- It's over, Knox.

1131
01:21:14,007 --> 01:21:15,175
Get up. We're leaving.

1132
01:21:15,242 --> 01:21:17,444
- I'm not going anywhere,
Marcus.

1133
01:21:18,780 --> 01:21:20,180
You have to kill me.

1134
01:21:21,048 --> 01:21:22,883
(Anderson): What happened,
Briggs?

1135
01:21:22,950 --> 01:21:25,620
(coughing)

1136
01:21:26,487 --> 01:21:30,424
I gave you a second chance
and you fucked it up all again.

1137
01:21:30,491 --> 01:21:32,660
(coughing)

1138
01:21:32,727 --> 01:21:35,630
- Fuck you, cunt.

1139
01:21:36,463 --> 01:21:37,632
(spits)

1140
01:21:42,704 --> 01:21:45,072
(coughing)

1141
01:21:50,010 --> 01:21:52,246
- I'm not saving
you again, Briggs.

1142
01:21:54,014 --> 01:21:55,850
(gunshot cracks)
- She sent me here

1143
01:21:55,916 --> 01:21:58,352
to pay her back
for the cover up.

1144
01:22:00,454 --> 01:22:03,758
At the time I felt like
I didn't have a choice.

1145
01:22:03,825 --> 01:22:05,492
- And you took over.

1146
01:22:05,560 --> 01:22:09,798
You took her chance
of profiting from this place.

1147
01:22:09,864 --> 01:22:10,964
From controlling it.

1148
01:22:11,031 --> 01:22:12,667
- The stream itself
was worth billions.

1149
01:22:14,536 --> 01:22:16,170
Anderson knew

1150
01:22:16,236 --> 01:22:19,072
she could run it
from the shadows.

1151
01:22:19,139 --> 01:22:21,776
- So, she sent Briggs
to clean up her mess.

1152
01:22:21,843 --> 01:22:22,911
- Precisely.

1153
01:22:22,976 --> 01:22:24,746
(footsteps approach)

1154
01:22:24,813 --> 01:22:27,816
- Marcus... put it down, Marcus.

1155
01:22:28,282 --> 01:22:30,284
(Marcus): You gonna
shoot me, Anderson?

1156
01:22:30,350 --> 01:22:33,053
- You killed Briggs.
You're a traitor.

1157
01:22:33,120 --> 01:22:35,022
- I had no choice.

1158
01:22:35,088 --> 01:22:36,825
You know that.

1159
01:22:37,391 --> 01:22:40,227
You know exactly what's
going on here, don't you?

1160
01:22:41,161 --> 01:22:43,096
- Do you wanna be a hero,

1161
01:22:43,163 --> 01:22:45,032
or do you wanna be
a terrorist like him?

1162
01:22:45,098 --> 01:22:47,735
- He's not a terrorist.

1163
01:22:47,802 --> 01:22:49,269
He's a SEAL.

1164
01:22:50,404 --> 01:22:52,774
Now I believe that he needs
to be held accountable

1165
01:22:52,841 --> 01:22:54,809
for the horrors of this place,

1166
01:22:54,876 --> 01:22:57,411
but he's no monster.

1167
01:22:57,478 --> 01:23:00,414
He's a product
of this environment.

1168
01:23:03,150 --> 01:23:05,920
We came here to rescue him
from this madness,

1169
01:23:05,986 --> 01:23:08,255
and we trusted you to help us!

1170
01:23:08,322 --> 01:23:10,457
(Anderson): It's bigger
than you think, Marcus.

1171
01:23:10,525 --> 01:23:13,494
You're not even scratching
the surface.

1172
01:23:14,361 --> 01:23:17,832
- I know it is,
and he's the key.

1173
01:23:17,899 --> 01:23:20,000
We need him.

1174
01:23:20,067 --> 01:23:23,437
- You're right, I do need him.

1175
01:23:25,640 --> 01:23:27,407
Knox,

1176
01:23:27,474 --> 01:23:29,544
did you really think
you could hide away

1177
01:23:29,611 --> 01:23:30,979
from me forever?

1178
01:23:31,044 --> 01:23:33,380
That I wouldn't come
catch up with you?

1179
01:23:33,447 --> 01:23:36,584
- I knew one day you'd send
your hounds after me.

1180
01:23:37,317 --> 01:23:39,052
I didn't think
I'd be lucky enough

1181
01:23:39,119 --> 01:23:40,688
to see you in person, though.

1182
01:23:41,455 --> 01:23:44,191
- You're gonna take me
to the server room,

1183
01:23:44,258 --> 01:23:47,595
and you're gonna give me
those passwords.

1184
01:23:48,696 --> 01:23:50,197
- Server room?

1185
01:23:53,200 --> 01:23:55,003
I don't even know where it is.

1186
01:23:55,068 --> 01:23:57,437
- I'm not asking you again!

1187
01:23:59,908 --> 01:24:04,411
- You know why you're no longer
a step ahead of me, Anderson?

1188
01:24:07,481 --> 01:24:10,618
Because fear is what
was holding me back.

1189
01:24:13,053 --> 01:24:16,558
The man you knew is dead

1190
01:24:16,624 --> 01:24:20,394
and the entity before you
is incapable of fear.

1191
01:24:22,429 --> 01:24:24,933
It doesn't fear humiliation,

1192
01:24:24,999 --> 01:24:27,569
failure, or death, like you do.

1193
01:24:31,138 --> 01:24:32,707
You can kill a man,

1194
01:24:34,842 --> 01:24:36,476
even a god,

1195
01:24:39,914 --> 01:24:42,349
but you can't kill an idea.

1196
01:24:44,284 --> 01:24:46,286
Isn't that right, Marcus?

1197
01:24:50,290 --> 01:24:53,761
But this is how
I kill you, Anderson.

1198
01:24:54,394 --> 01:24:56,931
(gunshot cracks)
- Knox! Knox!

1199
01:24:56,998 --> 01:24:58,365
(sounds muffle)

1200
01:24:58,432 --> 01:25:01,603
<i>(Knox): You're protectors</i>
<i>of gods.</i>

1201
01:25:09,844 --> 01:25:12,379
(Anderson panting)

1202
01:25:13,548 --> 01:25:15,917
- It's over, Anderson.
- You little fuck.

1203
01:25:15,984 --> 01:25:18,620
(grunting)

1204
01:25:29,697 --> 01:25:31,398
(blood spurting)

1205
01:25:33,735 --> 01:25:34,669
(grunts)

1206
01:25:36,804 --> 01:25:38,706
(lands punches)

1207
01:25:45,747 --> 01:25:47,314
(Marcus groans)

1208
01:25:50,183 --> 01:25:51,819
(coughing, gasping)

1209
01:25:56,057 --> 01:25:57,692
(panicked groaning)

1210
01:26:00,028 --> 01:26:01,996
- This is for Knox.

1211
01:26:02,063 --> 01:26:04,331
(blood spurts)

1212
01:26:06,067 --> 01:26:08,636
(choking, gasping)

1213
01:26:23,985 --> 01:26:25,620
Are you a wolf?

1214
01:26:28,890 --> 01:26:29,824
- Yes.

1215
01:26:31,358 --> 01:26:33,761
- Then we have work to do.

1216
01:26:41,536 --> 01:26:43,738
(ominous music peaks
and fades quickly)

1217
01:26:46,774 --> 01:26:49,811
<i>(Marcus): I sometimes dream</i>
<i>that I'm in a tunnel.</i>

1218
01:26:49,877 --> 01:26:51,713
(soft music)

1219
01:26:53,346 --> 01:26:55,783
<i>The way behind me is crumbling.</i>

1220
01:26:58,853 --> 01:27:02,924
<i>And so, I have no choice but</i>
<i>to move forward into the light.</i>

1221
01:27:04,859 --> 01:27:07,929
<i>But I don't know</i>
<i>what's waiting for me there.</i>

1222
01:27:07,995 --> 01:27:09,597
(insects chirping)

1223
01:27:13,968 --> 01:27:15,970
(phone buzzing)

1224
01:27:18,106 --> 01:27:19,807
(call beeps on)

1225
01:27:23,678 --> 01:27:27,815
- Yes. I have everything
prepared for what's to come.

1226
01:27:31,284 --> 01:27:32,954
It's truly an honor.

1227
01:27:33,020 --> 01:27:34,789
I won't let you down.

1228
01:27:38,993 --> 01:27:40,762
(grunting)

1229
01:27:48,169 --> 01:27:50,437
(breathing heavily)

1230
01:27:57,145 --> 01:27:59,547
(tense music)

1231
01:28:02,517 --> 01:28:04,952
I'm a United States General.

1232
01:28:06,286 --> 01:28:08,455
You must have a death wish.

1233
01:28:08,890 --> 01:28:10,024
(grunts)

1234
01:28:10,091 --> 01:28:11,993
- How ironic.

1235
01:28:12,059 --> 01:28:13,895
(mocking laugh)

1236
01:28:14,762 --> 01:28:16,864
- You don't know the half
of who you're dealing with.

1237
01:28:19,366 --> 01:28:21,068
They'll never let you live.

1238
01:28:21,636 --> 01:28:25,706
- Well, that's fine,
'cause we're already dead.

1239
01:28:26,439 --> 01:28:29,744
(sweeping instrumental music)

1240
01:28:31,846 --> 01:28:35,583
<i>(Marcus): My father showed me</i>
<i>how to be a man.</i>

1241
01:28:36,383 --> 01:28:40,353
<i>But after all</i>
<i>the monsters I've seen,</i>

1242
01:28:40,420 --> 01:28:43,024
<i>I can only be the wolf.</i>

1243
01:29:02,210 --> 01:29:04,979
(ominous music)